WEBVTT

1
00:00:53.971 --> 00:00:55.990
You said you knew where she was going.

2
00:00:56.014 --> 00:00:59.494
- I did. She got away.
- From you.

3
00:00:59.518 --> 00:01:02.038
She was helped
by one of her Mechanical friends.

4
00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:04.581
I chased them.
but they got down here first

5
00:01:04.605 --> 00:01:07.067
and disappeared
before I could get a chair.

6
00:01:09.027 --> 00:01:10.821
You already knew I was down here.

7
00:01:12.489 --> 00:01:15.492
People take notice
of where you go. Robert.

8
00:01:16.201 --> 00:01:18.328
You know what? I'll take it from here.

9
00:01:18.996 --> 00:01:21.182
I know Greasetown. And it's still on edge.

10
00:01:21.206 --> 00:01:23.184
I've got Jo and Chad.
I think I can manage.

11
00:01:23.208 --> 00:01:24.751
I should be here for you.

12
00:01:26.128 --> 00:01:27.880
- We could split up.
- Go home to Anthony.

13
00:01:29.882 --> 00:01:31.175
Spend time with him.

14
00:01:32.259 --> 00:01:34.112
It doesn't have to come to that.

15
00:01:34.136 --> 00:01:36.221
It will if I can't find her.

16
00:01:43.562 --> 00:01:46.207
Camille Sims for Emerson.
I'm below the gap.

17
00:01:46.231 --> 00:01:48.001
When Nichols was a fugitive.
she was caught down here.

18
00:01:48.025 --> 00:01:49.127
Find out where.

19
00:01:49.151 --> 00:01:50.903
And Judge Sims is headed up.

20
00:01:51.612 --> 00:01:52.905
Keep eyes on him...

21
00:01:53.572 --> 00:01:55.657
- for his safety.
- <i>Copy that</i>.

22
00:02:03.415 --> 00:02:04.583
I need to lie down.

23
00:02:06.627 --> 00:02:07.961
Have some water.

24
00:02:08.544 --> 00:02:12.424
The actual fuck? You're alive?

25
00:02:13.175 --> 00:02:14.426
He's alive?

26
00:02:21.391 --> 00:02:22.434
Here.

27
00:02:24.269 --> 00:02:26.104
Anybody else coming back from the dead?

28
00:02:26.647 --> 00:02:28.148
The old sheriff. maybe his wife?

29
00:02:29.107 --> 00:02:30.442
Did anybody see you?

30
00:02:31.777 --> 00:02:33.195
Just Teddy.

31
00:02:35.614 --> 00:02:36.865
Mr. Kyle.

32
00:02:37.824 --> 00:02:38.909
Mr. Holland.

33
00:02:39.743 --> 00:02:43.330
I'm very glad you're still alive.

34
00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:50.730
I didn't think you'd survive the move.

35
00:02:50.754 --> 00:02:54.842
Isn't there a small part of you
that's happy to see me again?

36
00:03:01.849 --> 00:03:04.852
I remember. I know what we have to do.

37
00:03:09.064 --> 00:03:10.607
<i>Emerson for Camille Sims</i>.

38
00:03:11.859 --> 00:03:13.753
- Go.
- The address you were looking for

39
00:03:13.777 --> 00:03:17.698
is a workshop on 144.
occupied by Martha Walker.

40
00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:24.680
One of the lines must have been a pipe.

41
00:03:26.373 --> 00:03:27.433
What?

42
00:03:27.457 --> 00:03:32.021
Mr. Kyle put the hard drive I smashed
back together.

43
00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:34.482
The diagram you found

44
00:03:34.506 --> 00:03:38.194
showed lines coming in from outside.

45
00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:42.115
There are two lines. One goes to IT.
and the other goes to Judicial.

46
00:03:42.139 --> 00:03:43.700
And I didn't know what the lines were.

47
00:03:43.724 --> 00:03:45.451
but that's why I went to the mines.

48
00:03:45.475 --> 00:03:46.661
Yeah. well. you're an idiot.

49
00:03:46.685 --> 00:03:49.956
They're not gonna put some killer pipe
where criminals dig all day.

50
00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:53.001
There are tunnels in the mines
that go up and down the Silo.

51
00:03:53.025 --> 00:03:55.336
And I almost made it
to the line that goes into IT

52
00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:56.671
when they gassed the mines.

53
00:03:56.695 --> 00:04:01.992
The lines going into IT
carry electricity from Silo 1.

54
00:04:02.492 --> 00:04:07.056
So if the generator stops
there's always power in IT.

55
00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:12.353
So. then the line that goes to Judicial.
that's the Safeguard.

56
00:04:12.377 --> 00:04:14.481
I think that's what he said. That's...

57
00:04:14.505 --> 00:04:16.524
- I think that's what Jimmy said.
- Now hold on. who is Jimmy?

58
00:04:16.548 --> 00:04:18.526
Jimmy is the guy that I was with in 17.

59
00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:20.195
That's what... I think that's what he said.

60
00:04:20.219 --> 00:04:25.891
Did this Jimmy tell you
where the lines entered into Judicial?

61
00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:31.230
<i>He had an old blueprint. but...</i>

62
00:04:36.777 --> 00:04:39.947
No. It... I can't... It's gone.

63
00:04:54.336 --> 00:04:55.897
Where's our blueprint?

64
00:04:55.921 --> 00:04:58.608
Look. if we have a blueprint.
it would be on that hard drive

65
00:04:58.632 --> 00:04:59.776
which is back in IT.

66
00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:01.444
We're not gonna get to that.

67
00:05:01.468 --> 00:05:04.531
Well. maybe your new pal. Sims.
can help us find it.

68
00:05:04.555 --> 00:05:05.782
Where is Sims?

69
00:05:05.806 --> 00:05:07.075
He went to head off Camille.

70
00:05:07.099 --> 00:05:10.203
Wait. Is 17 the same as our silo?

71
00:05:10.227 --> 00:05:11.871
Yeah. they're exactly the same.

72
00:05:11.895 --> 00:05:15.416
So. then if we find the pipe in 17.
we find it here.

73
00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.710
Is there a way to communicate with Jimmy?

74
00:05:17.734 --> 00:05:20.672
Every silo has its own frequency.
so I can try to...

75
00:05:20.696 --> 00:05:24.449
I never saw him with a radio.
I never found a radio. I...

76
00:05:25.075 --> 00:05:26.886
Camille Sims is coming this way.

77
00:05:26.910 --> 00:05:27.971
Shit.

78
00:05:27.995 --> 00:05:30.163
We're gonna have to move you again.

79
00:05:31.290 --> 00:05:33.166
- Go.
- Shit.

80
00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:36.253
You serious?

81
00:05:37.254 --> 00:05:38.690
How long do we have?

82
00:05:38.714 --> 00:05:40.733
McLain said when she became Head of Supply

83
00:05:40.757 --> 00:05:43.653
we had 70 years of light bulbs left.

84
00:05:43.677 --> 00:05:46.805
Since someone started stealing them.
it's down to two.

85
00:05:50.559 --> 00:05:51.810
What do we do?

86
00:05:53.812 --> 00:05:56.457
First. we keep this to ourselves.

87
00:05:56.481 --> 00:05:58.418
It's only been three months
since one rebellion.

88
00:05:58.442 --> 00:05:59.651
we can't have another one.

89
00:06:00.986 --> 00:06:03.238
Then we find out who killed Orla Kent.

90
00:06:03.906 --> 00:06:07.135
When we do. we might find out
who stole the light bulbs.

91
00:06:07.159 --> 00:06:09.971
Or if we find out who's
been stealing light bulbs.

92
00:06:09.995 --> 00:06:12.039
maybe we find out who killed Orla Kent.

93
00:06:38.649 --> 00:06:40.317
Before you arrest me. we should talk.

94
00:06:41.235 --> 00:06:42.736
Somewhere with no cameras.

95
00:06:45.239 --> 00:06:48.158
I remember everything.

96
00:08:49.905 --> 00:08:51.841
- Fuck.
- Fuck what?

97
00:08:51.865 --> 00:08:53.343
We're now going 70.

98
00:08:53.367 --> 00:08:55.803
We probably should have tried to jump out
when we were still in the city.

99
00:08:55.827 --> 00:08:59.015
I said that. and then you said
that we would die even at 40.

100
00:08:59.039 --> 00:09:00.517
Only horribly injured.

101
00:09:00.541 --> 00:09:03.061
But now. we'd definitely just be a smear.

102
00:09:03.085 --> 00:09:05.772
Can you just try
taking out the key? Please.

103
00:09:05.796 --> 00:09:06.797
No.

104
00:09:12.177 --> 00:09:14.405
- Hey. What?
- If we get the fob away from the van.

105
00:09:14.429 --> 00:09:17.158
- won't it just stop working?
- I hope not.

106
00:09:17.182 --> 00:09:19.810
Your kid tosses it.
and you shut down in the middle of I-95?

107
00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:21.371
Not safe.

108
00:09:21.395 --> 00:09:24.332
Safe is not what
I'm fucking feeling right now.

109
00:09:24.356 --> 00:09:26.376
No brakes. No steering.

110
00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:28.670
This is like what
happened to Charlotte's squadron.

111
00:09:28.694 --> 00:09:30.588
You think someone in Iran is driving this?

112
00:09:30.612 --> 00:09:31.905
I don't know. but someone is.

113
00:09:33.323 --> 00:09:37.262
Stensen's been sounding the alarm
on how AI can be used by hackers. right?

114
00:09:37.286 --> 00:09:38.680
So maybe he was on the <i>Nimitz</i>

115
00:09:38.704 --> 00:09:41.290
because he feared
the planes would be compromised.

116
00:09:41.832 --> 00:09:43.083
And they were.

117
00:09:44.585 --> 00:09:45.794
Too crazy?

118
00:09:47.171 --> 00:09:48.839
I think we're neck-deep in crazy.

119
00:09:52.593 --> 00:09:54.928
I need something with a flat edge.

120
00:10:03.395 --> 00:10:04.396
Damn it.

121
00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:17.701
Here.

122
00:10:33.550 --> 00:10:35.385
Do you actually know what you're doing?

123
00:10:35.928 --> 00:10:38.222
Roughly. Brakes are simple.

124
00:10:38.722 --> 00:10:44.287
You step on a pedal. it activates a line
which makes the brake pads squeeze.

125
00:10:44.311 --> 00:10:46.164
But whoever's driving this.

126
00:10:46.188 --> 00:10:48.666
is doing something
with the electronics to stop that.

127
00:10:48.690 --> 00:10:50.418
So. if I can access the...

128
00:10:50.442 --> 00:10:51.527
- What?
- Fuck!

129
00:10:54.196 --> 00:10:55.280
Damn it.

130
00:11:01.119 --> 00:11:02.120
Let me see.

131
00:11:14.091 --> 00:11:15.300
Think you'll live?

132
00:11:16.134 --> 00:11:17.135
Sure hope so.

133
00:11:24.852 --> 00:11:26.186
I know about the voice.

134
00:11:27.771 --> 00:11:29.398
- What voice?
- No. don't do that.

135
00:11:30.983 --> 00:11:32.818
I'm not gonna talk to you about this.

136
00:11:34.069 --> 00:11:36.655
Camille. you know I didn't go
into a refuge hut.

137
00:11:37.281 --> 00:11:41.410
I don't know what it tells you.
but I went into another silo.

138
00:11:43.996 --> 00:11:46.748
It's not dead. There are kids in it.

139
00:11:47.291 --> 00:11:49.936
And they're alone. and somehow
they've managed to survive.

140
00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:52.313
But I promised them
that I would go back to them.

141
00:11:52.337 --> 00:11:53.940
That's what I remember.

142
00:11:53.964 --> 00:11:56.526
I remember that I said
I would bring them back here.

143
00:11:56.550 --> 00:12:00.697
- That's an insane request.
- Let me ask the voice. and it can decide.

144
00:12:00.721 --> 00:12:01.763
No.

145
00:12:04.933 --> 00:12:07.144
You know people treat me
like a living Founder.

146
00:12:07.769 --> 00:12:09.563
If I jump off the stairs. they'll follow.

147
00:12:11.064 --> 00:12:13.144
You wanna see what else
they're willing to do for me?

148
00:12:13.483 --> 00:12:15.712
You sound like a threat to the Silo.

149
00:12:15.736 --> 00:12:20.449
No. Camille. I want to save the kids.

150
00:12:28.165 --> 00:12:31.084
You sure there are no cameras here?
It looks like it knows we're talking.

151
00:12:44.389 --> 00:12:46.308
- Any luck?
- No.

152
00:12:47.392 --> 00:12:49.603
There has to be some way
to stop this thing.

153
00:12:53.190 --> 00:12:54.626
What?

154
00:12:54.650 --> 00:12:59.172
Hey. hey. hey! Hey! Stop! Call the police!

155
00:12:59.196 --> 00:13:01.615
Help. help. help. help!
Stop. stop. stop. stop!

156
00:13:02.199 --> 00:13:07.037
Please. please. please!
Call the police! Stop! Hey!

157
00:13:10.165 --> 00:13:11.333
What the fuck?

158
00:13:13.126 --> 00:13:14.378
What happened?

159
00:13:17.714 --> 00:13:19.234
I think I know how to stop this thing.

160
00:13:20.926 --> 00:13:24.155
Hank. I make things. I don't steal them.

161
00:13:24.179 --> 00:13:26.366
We're just hoping
you know somebody who does.

162
00:13:26.390 --> 00:13:29.869
I only associate
with Pact-abiding citizens. you know that.

163
00:13:29.893 --> 00:13:33.665
Mark. we... we've got something
pretty serious going on.

164
00:13:33.689 --> 00:13:35.375
We could really use your help.

165
00:13:35.399 --> 00:13:38.336
Serious. like getting chucked
over the rail?

166
00:13:38.360 --> 00:13:41.714
There are two raiders guilty of throwing
my best friend to his death

167
00:13:41.738 --> 00:13:43.299
during the rebellion.

168
00:13:43.323 --> 00:13:45.510
But I don't hear you asking about that.

169
00:13:45.534 --> 00:13:49.371
This friend of yours.
was his name Lee Torgenson?

170
00:13:50.330 --> 00:13:52.892
And was he thrown over
for using a weapon you made for him?

171
00:13:52.916 --> 00:13:55.627
- Fuck you. Who the fuck are you?
- I'm the sheriff.

172
00:13:56.170 --> 00:13:58.356
- And if you don't cooperate. we...
- You're not a sheriff.

173
00:13:58.380 --> 00:14:00.150
- You're an accident.
- Mark.

174
00:14:00.174 --> 00:14:01.401
You got the job by default.

175
00:14:01.425 --> 00:14:03.820
Now you're standing here
wearing Holston's hand-me-downs.

176
00:14:03.844 --> 00:14:05.738
and they're one size too big.

177
00:14:05.762 --> 00:14:07.073
You wanna arrest someone?

178
00:14:07.097 --> 00:14:08.825
- Arrest your wife.
- Mark!

179
00:14:08.849 --> 00:14:11.202
You think people don't know
about her and the Outsiders?

180
00:14:11.226 --> 00:14:12.996
Trying to get us all killed?

181
00:14:13.020 --> 00:14:16.064
What are you going to do. Mr. Sheriff?
Drag me out of here?

182
00:14:16.857 --> 00:14:18.108
That'll look great.

183
00:14:21.486 --> 00:14:22.946
Mark. we are not threatening you.

184
00:14:23.572 --> 00:14:26.050
We're just in a tough spot.
and we really need to know

185
00:14:26.074 --> 00:14:29.929
if anyone has info on things
disappearing from Critical Supply.

186
00:14:29.953 --> 00:14:32.456
I'm not doing shit for this asshole.

187
00:14:37.794 --> 00:14:39.213
How about this...

188
00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:45.052
You give us something we can use.
and I'll look into the raiders.

189
00:14:46.178 --> 00:14:47.906
- You won't do anything...
- I'll get their names.

190
00:14:47.930 --> 00:14:51.767
I'll give them to you. Whatever you do
with that information is up to you.

191
00:15:05.113 --> 00:15:06.114
All right.

192
00:15:08.158 --> 00:15:12.663
Here's this...
The weapons I made. I made for Knox.

193
00:15:13.247 --> 00:15:15.082
You wanna know about stolen shit?

194
00:15:16.416 --> 00:15:18.460
His father was crooked as a screw.

195
00:15:19.419 --> 00:15:21.397
He used to steal
diamond drill bits from Supply.

196
00:15:21.421 --> 00:15:23.173
and sold 'em on the black market
as jewelry.

197
00:15:23.924 --> 00:15:25.676
Far as I know. he's out of that game.

198
00:15:26.426 --> 00:15:28.136
But he'll know more than I will.

199
00:15:28.720 --> 00:15:30.264
That something you can use?

200
00:15:36.436 --> 00:15:37.604
Get me those names.

201
00:15:39.523 --> 00:15:41.233
- You all right?
- I'm fine.

202
00:15:52.953 --> 00:15:55.414
We just sit. and we wait.

203
00:15:56.206 --> 00:15:58.101
Come on. All it takes is one person

204
00:15:58.125 --> 00:16:01.712
to see an empty van driving by itself.
and they will call the cops.

205
00:16:04.798 --> 00:16:07.384
Ye of little faith.

206
00:16:34.119 --> 00:16:37.456
<i>Juliette Nichols. why are you here?</i>

207
00:16:43.837 --> 00:16:45.005
You just speak.

208
00:16:46.548 --> 00:16:47.674
Okay.

209
00:16:49.843 --> 00:16:52.054
I know what happened when I went outside.

210
00:16:52.721 --> 00:16:58.143
And... In Silo 17 there are kids.
and I want to bring them back. Here.

211
00:17:03.190 --> 00:17:06.026
Silo 17 is flooding. and they're gonna die.

212
00:17:10.614 --> 00:17:14.785
I'm not working against the Silo.
I'm not working against you.

213
00:17:15.827 --> 00:17:17.204
I'm not a threat.

214
00:17:22.459 --> 00:17:25.563
<i>The numbers predict
disaster for the Silo if you leave.</i>

215
00:17:25.587 --> 00:17:27.023
<i>Request is denied.</i>

216
00:17:27.047 --> 00:17:29.818
No. not me.
We'll send someone else to get them.

217
00:17:29.842 --> 00:17:31.277
<i>The numbers predict disaster</i>

218
00:17:31.301 --> 00:17:34.304
<i>if residents from another silo join Silo 18</i>.

219
00:17:35.430 --> 00:17:36.783
<i>Request is denied</i>.

220
00:17:36.807 --> 00:17:40.143
No. but they're kids.
They're gonna die in 17.

221
00:17:41.895 --> 00:17:45.333
<i>They'd be invasive. Request is denied.</i>

222
00:17:45.357 --> 00:17:47.776
Time to leave. Come on.

223
00:17:54.992 --> 00:17:58.745
Okay. what if I go back on
the memory drug? Is that what you want?

224
00:17:59.872 --> 00:18:01.123
I'll do it.

225
00:18:05.586 --> 00:18:07.838
You can even drug the kids.

226
00:18:10.382 --> 00:18:12.502
And then they won't be a threat
to anyone here. right?

227
00:18:18.640 --> 00:18:20.058
<i>How many children?</i>

228
00:18:28.775 --> 00:18:30.527
I think you're making a play.

229
00:18:31.695 --> 00:18:32.905
- I'm not.
- You're not?

230
00:18:34.364 --> 00:18:37.552
- You have my word.
- I have your word. really?

231
00:18:37.576 --> 00:18:39.536
You lied to me.

232
00:18:40.162 --> 00:18:45.584
You drugged me for three fucking months.
and you question my honesty?

233
00:18:48.795 --> 00:18:52.716
I'll find someone to get the kids.
and then I'll go back to being your mayor.

234
00:19:05.270 --> 00:19:06.271
What?

235
00:19:06.813 --> 00:19:08.732
We're in the middle of fucking nowhere.

236
00:19:11.068 --> 00:19:14.547
Don't rental cars have.
like... locator things?

237
00:19:14.571 --> 00:19:17.574
I got this from Joe's sketchy car rental.
There's no locator.

238
00:19:20.994 --> 00:19:23.556
You're a congressman.
so people are gonna notice

239
00:19:23.580 --> 00:19:24.974
if you don't show up for work.

240
00:19:24.998 --> 00:19:26.768
Not for at least a day.

241
00:19:26.792 --> 00:19:29.837
They'll just be glad I'm not babbling
about infrastructure reform.

242
00:19:30.963 --> 00:19:31.964
What about Charlotte?

243
00:19:34.883 --> 00:19:37.695
Saw her a couple of days ago.
she barely knew who I was.

244
00:19:37.719 --> 00:19:40.198
And Crnkovich asked me
to stay away for a little bit

245
00:19:40.222 --> 00:19:41.932
while she gets focused therapy.

246
00:19:43.016 --> 00:19:44.977
But. he said she is doing better. so...

247
00:19:45.853 --> 00:19:46.854
There's that.

248
00:19:51.024 --> 00:19:54.152
You? Any potential rescuers
in your corner?

249
00:19:55.988 --> 00:19:57.447
I mean...

250
00:19:58.866 --> 00:20:03.662
I got fired. so nobody there
is expecting to see me ever again.

251
00:20:05.914 --> 00:20:08.667
And I am a pretty shitty friend.

252
00:20:11.170 --> 00:20:13.338
It takes me weeks to call anyone back.

253
00:20:15.340 --> 00:20:16.341
So. no.

254
00:20:24.016 --> 00:20:25.118
- You know...
- What?

255
00:20:25.142 --> 00:20:28.121
If they did just want to kill us.
they've had plenty of opportunities.

256
00:20:28.145 --> 00:20:30.582
They could have driven us
into a bridge abutment

257
00:20:30.606 --> 00:20:33.042
or off a cliff. or into a tree.

258
00:20:33.066 --> 00:20:34.735
But they haven't. which. you know.

259
00:20:35.611 --> 00:20:38.197
leaves the possibility
we could be going someplace nice.

260
00:20:47.915 --> 00:20:49.291
We are so fucked.

261
00:21:07.559 --> 00:21:08.936
Where's Lukas and Kennedy?

262
00:21:10.270 --> 00:21:12.081
Kennedy just wouldn't stop talking.

263
00:21:12.105 --> 00:21:16.878
He needs a rest. so. I found them
an empty single down the hallway.

264
00:21:16.902 --> 00:21:18.588
- Good.
- Where did you go?

265
00:21:18.612 --> 00:21:20.113
I went with Camille.

266
00:21:20.697 --> 00:21:23.825
To the Vault. I... I spoke to it.

267
00:21:25.369 --> 00:21:26.679
What did you say?

268
00:21:26.703 --> 00:21:31.184
I said I wanna send two people to 17.
and bring the kids back here.

269
00:21:31.208 --> 00:21:32.584
And it believed you?

270
00:21:33.168 --> 00:21:34.229
I think so.

271
00:21:34.253 --> 00:21:38.507
- Is it a person. or a machine?
- I don't know.

272
00:21:40.008 --> 00:21:41.385
So who you gonna send?

273
00:21:44.429 --> 00:21:46.449
You know. when I went out
I didn't have a choice.

274
00:21:46.473 --> 00:21:48.058
I had to keep going. Right?

275
00:21:49.184 --> 00:21:53.480
There are hundreds.
There are thousands of bodies out there.

276
00:21:54.273 --> 00:21:57.710
So. whoever we send have
to be able to walk through that.

277
00:21:57.734 --> 00:21:59.319
and not wanna turn back.

278
00:22:00.487 --> 00:22:02.407
If I had the choice.
I don't think I could do it.

279
00:22:03.657 --> 00:22:05.635
So. they better be strong.

280
00:22:05.659 --> 00:22:06.660
Yeah.

281
00:22:07.160 --> 00:22:08.388
And they've gotta be smart.

282
00:22:08.412 --> 00:22:11.290
They've gotta find that pipe.
They've gotta figure out how to cap it.

283
00:22:12.082 --> 00:22:14.209
They need to be engineers.

284
00:22:15.794 --> 00:22:17.379
The best you have.

285
00:22:25.220 --> 00:22:26.555
Ask.

286
00:22:27.139 --> 00:22:29.016
They can always say no.

287
00:22:38.358 --> 00:22:40.277
Shirl. what's going on?

288
00:22:40.903 --> 00:22:42.613
- Why don't you sit down?
- No. it's...

289
00:22:50.078 --> 00:22:52.998
I can't stop thinking
all of us could be gone.

290
00:22:55.751 --> 00:22:58.480
Before we ever get a chance to...

291
00:22:58.504 --> 00:22:59.505
I know.

292
00:23:00.547 --> 00:23:02.382
But we can't think like that.

293
00:23:04.843 --> 00:23:07.322
We just have to focus on...

294
00:23:07.346 --> 00:23:08.680
on what we can do.

295
00:23:22.444 --> 00:23:23.737
Knox.

296
00:23:25.906 --> 00:23:27.366
I need a word with you.

297
00:23:32.663 --> 00:23:33.723
About what?

298
00:23:33.747 --> 00:23:34.957
Your father.

299
00:23:38.627 --> 00:23:40.021
This is not a good time.

300
00:23:40.045 --> 00:23:41.356
Yeah. it'll just take a minute.

301
00:23:41.380 --> 00:23:43.983
What do you know about his connection
to the market in stolen goods?

302
00:23:44.007 --> 00:23:45.401
I'm not doing this right now.

303
00:23:45.425 --> 00:23:46.861
- Why not?
- 'Cause I'm not.

304
00:23:46.885 --> 00:23:48.238
Are you trying to protect him?

305
00:23:48.262 --> 00:23:50.532
Are you fucking kidding me?
Are you really asking me that?

306
00:23:50.556 --> 00:23:52.724
- Yes. I am because if you are...
- What?

307
00:23:54.518 --> 00:23:55.894
What are you gonna do?

308
00:23:57.938 --> 00:23:59.874
- You think that badge means shit to me?
- Hank.

309
00:23:59.898 --> 00:24:02.210
All right. Just calm down.

310
00:24:02.234 --> 00:24:03.277
All right?

311
00:24:03.777 --> 00:24:05.487
This is about a murder.

312
00:24:06.530 --> 00:24:08.615
- Who?
- Orla Kent.

313
00:24:09.449 --> 00:24:11.553
- I don't know her.
- The hell you don't.

314
00:24:11.577 --> 00:24:14.597
She was the shadow to the head of Supply.
She was at the Silo Council...

315
00:24:14.621 --> 00:24:16.766
If I say I don't her.
then I don't fucking know her.

316
00:24:16.790 --> 00:24:20.395
Like you apparently don't know me.
Get him the fuck out of here. Hank.

317
00:24:20.419 --> 00:24:21.896
- Move. Let me the fuck at...
- No.

318
00:24:21.920 --> 00:24:22.981
Leave it. Just. don't.

319
00:24:23.005 --> 00:24:25.507
Not now. Just. trust me. Not now.

320
00:24:26.216 --> 00:24:27.342
Trust me.

321
00:24:38.520 --> 00:24:41.124
Hey. Look. you told me
Harwood had a run-in

322
00:24:41.148 --> 00:24:42.834
with Orla Kent at the Council meeting.

323
00:24:42.858 --> 00:24:45.587
Right? You said McLain was suspicious

324
00:24:45.611 --> 00:24:47.380
of Harwood's daughter
when she was shadowing her...

325
00:24:47.404 --> 00:24:48.381
- Glenda.
- Yeah.

326
00:24:48.405 --> 00:24:50.490
Already spoke to her.
Got nothing concrete.

327
00:24:55.120 --> 00:24:57.080
But maybe we can track her movements.

328
00:24:59.041 --> 00:25:00.083
And Orla's.

329
00:25:00.584 --> 00:25:01.728
Track them?

330
00:25:01.752 --> 00:25:02.920
How?

331
00:25:10.344 --> 00:25:11.404
What do you want?

332
00:25:11.428 --> 00:25:13.198
Where do you watch the cameras?

333
00:25:13.222 --> 00:25:14.515
Nowhere.

334
00:25:18.477 --> 00:25:21.271
There was a room on 19.
but they've shut it down.

335
00:25:21.897 --> 00:25:25.025
I've been rewriting the Pact.
and I know nothing's changed.

336
00:25:28.529 --> 00:25:29.655
Take us.

337
00:25:32.783 --> 00:25:33.992
What is that?

338
00:25:35.369 --> 00:25:39.998
There was a relic I
kept in my pocket for...

339
00:25:40.707 --> 00:25:42.602
years.

340
00:25:42.626 --> 00:25:49.466
Records said that it was found
in a pillowcase a long time ago.

341
00:25:52.135 --> 00:25:54.346
They called such things...

342
00:25:55.472 --> 00:25:58.725
good luck charms.

343
00:25:59.226 --> 00:26:00.686
Well. did it work?

344
00:26:01.854 --> 00:26:07.985
Well. the relic burned
along with some of me. so maybe not.

345
00:26:10.904 --> 00:26:13.091
That said. I'm still alive.

346
00:26:13.115 --> 00:26:17.637
Although. I'm not sure that's good luck.

347
00:26:17.661 --> 00:26:18.954
Boo-hoo.

348
00:26:20.038 --> 00:26:21.808
You're being waited on hand and foot.

349
00:26:21.832 --> 00:26:24.960
All you have to do
is lie back and pontificate.

350
00:26:36.096 --> 00:26:37.973
Why did you keep me alive?

351
00:26:38.724 --> 00:26:42.662
You convinced Sims not to kill Juliette.

352
00:26:42.686 --> 00:26:44.062
I know.

353
00:26:45.272 --> 00:26:46.440
It's just...

354
00:26:48.692 --> 00:26:50.044
It can't have been easy.

355
00:26:50.068 --> 00:26:51.153
No.

356
00:26:52.571 --> 00:26:54.549
And you're still a rat shit asshole.

357
00:26:54.573 --> 00:26:56.676
You shouldn't be surprised
if you wake up one morning

358
00:26:56.700 --> 00:26:58.386
with a screwdriver in your neck.

359
00:26:58.410 --> 00:27:01.079
Even as a boy they wanted me dead.

360
00:27:02.623 --> 00:27:04.291
That wasn't a joke.

361
00:27:05.792 --> 00:27:07.753
I was always...

362
00:27:08.504 --> 00:27:11.089
too smart and...

363
00:27:12.382 --> 00:27:14.718
too quiet.

364
00:27:23.685 --> 00:27:25.288
What's so amusing?

365
00:27:25.312 --> 00:27:27.457
It's just...

366
00:27:27.481 --> 00:27:29.274
It's just something Carla said.

367
00:27:30.484 --> 00:27:33.505
She said if I liked men.
and you liked people.

368
00:27:33.529 --> 00:27:34.988
we'd make a great couple.

369
00:27:37.115 --> 00:27:38.492
That is amusing.

370
00:27:57.010 --> 00:27:58.762
I wanted to apologize.

371
00:27:59.888 --> 00:28:01.139
Now you don't?

372
00:28:06.562 --> 00:28:07.622
It's the wrong tense.

373
00:28:07.646 --> 00:28:10.208
If you actually want to apologize.
it's "I want..."

374
00:28:10.232 --> 00:28:13.127
I want... want to apologize.

375
00:28:13.151 --> 00:28:14.278
Present tense.

376
00:28:15.612 --> 00:28:19.032
For what I said about journalistic fraud.

377
00:28:25.706 --> 00:28:26.707
What happened?

378
00:28:28.041 --> 00:28:29.602
You really didn't look it up?

379
00:28:29.626 --> 00:28:31.879
I just saw there was some thing
at the <i>Post.</i>

380
00:28:32.504 --> 00:28:35.942
"Thing at the <i>Post</i>" makes it sound like
I wore white to a wedding.

381
00:28:35.966 --> 00:28:37.885
I started to read it. and then...

382
00:28:40.012 --> 00:28:41.263
You made something up.

383
00:28:49.521 --> 00:28:54.943
I did a piece on drug addiction
among congressional staffers.

384
00:28:56.320 --> 00:28:58.822
Yeah. I was careful.

385
00:29:00.073 --> 00:29:01.593
I changed everyone's details

386
00:29:01.617 --> 00:29:04.995
'cause I knew people would try
and read between the lines.

387
00:29:06.163 --> 00:29:07.956
And I wanted to protect my sources.

388
00:29:08.832 --> 00:29:10.250
Protect their anonymity...

389
00:29:11.335 --> 00:29:13.980
but the day it was published.

390
00:29:14.004 --> 00:29:18.759
a quote from a young woman
I called Sharon got everybody talking.

391
00:29:20.636 --> 00:29:21.762
I knew it would.

392
00:29:23.388 --> 00:29:26.683
She implied that drug use
was not limited to staffers.

393
00:29:28.519 --> 00:29:32.272
Rumors. you know. spread
that the Speaker was using.

394
00:29:33.649 --> 00:29:36.568
You can imagine the pressure
to reveal Sharon's identity.

395
00:29:37.611 --> 00:29:41.448
Legislators. prosecutors.
Capitol police. all...

396
00:29:42.407 --> 00:29:45.118
demanding I reveal her real name.

397
00:29:47.704 --> 00:29:50.975
And then those fuck-nuts at
the <i>Washingtonian</i> published a piece saying

398
00:29:50.999 --> 00:29:55.337
Sharon was really Gillian Aikens
who worked in the Speaker's office.

399
00:29:58.924 --> 00:30:00.384
Problem was they were right.

400
00:30:02.636 --> 00:30:03.637
So what did you do?

401
00:30:05.681 --> 00:30:07.099
Only thing I could do.

402
00:30:08.392 --> 00:30:09.869
I published a tearful confession.

403
00:30:09.893 --> 00:30:14.499
said I'd heard some
utterly spurious rumors about the Speaker.

404
00:30:14.523 --> 00:30:17.025
and had made up Sharon.

405
00:30:18.277 --> 00:30:20.571
You gave up your career
to protect a source?

406
00:30:21.154 --> 00:30:23.407
I gave up my career
because I failed Gillian.

407
00:30:26.451 --> 00:30:27.703
If I'd done a better job...

408
00:30:29.496 --> 00:30:31.206
her name would have never come up.

409
00:30:45.137 --> 00:30:46.180
No.

410
00:30:47.181 --> 00:30:48.408
What?

411
00:30:48.432 --> 00:30:50.392
You're not going to 17.

412
00:30:51.602 --> 00:30:52.662
I'll go alone.

413
00:30:52.686 --> 00:30:54.539
You can't go alone. No one can.

414
00:30:54.563 --> 00:30:56.857
- Why not?
- In case one of us doesn't make it.

415
00:30:57.566 --> 00:31:00.152
Then Teddy will come with me.

416
00:31:00.986 --> 00:31:03.363
Jules. could you just give us a second?

417
00:31:05.824 --> 00:31:07.260
I need to make a move.

418
00:31:07.284 --> 00:31:08.785
It won't take long.

419
00:31:17.878 --> 00:31:19.439
I'll tell her.

420
00:31:19.463 --> 00:31:20.815
And if I do that. she'll never let...

421
00:31:20.839 --> 00:31:24.259
You tell her. and I raise this kid alone.

422
00:31:26.261 --> 00:31:30.974
We don't do this. our kid
and everyone in here will never be safe.

423
00:31:32.351 --> 00:31:33.810
Shirl. please.

424
00:31:34.478 --> 00:31:36.021
Let me take someone else.

425
00:31:36.730 --> 00:31:37.856
It's not the same.

426
00:31:38.690 --> 00:31:39.858
You know that.

427
00:31:40.651 --> 00:31:42.611
If you were Jules. who would you send?

428
00:31:45.948 --> 00:31:47.282
Fuck!

429
00:32:11.723 --> 00:32:13.141
It has to be us.

430
00:32:14.476 --> 00:32:15.477
Both of us.

431
00:32:22.276 --> 00:32:23.920
We do this...

432
00:32:23.944 --> 00:32:26.238
and something happens to you.

433
00:32:26.822 --> 00:32:30.075
Something happens...

434
00:32:33.704 --> 00:32:35.581
It's different now. I don't...

435
00:32:38.834 --> 00:32:40.627
I don't know if I'd come back from that.

436
00:32:44.214 --> 00:32:46.359
When we were on our way up
to see the judge.

437
00:32:46.383 --> 00:32:50.179
you said you wanted
to go out to see the distance.

438
00:32:53.807 --> 00:32:55.350
At least we'll see it together.

439
00:33:14.620 --> 00:33:20.059
You have to promise me.
if I go down. you just keep going.

440
00:33:20.083 --> 00:33:21.752
You don't stop. You don't...

441
00:33:22.419 --> 00:33:24.505
You don't try and save me.

442
00:33:28.217 --> 00:33:29.343
You just go.

443
00:33:38.894 --> 00:33:39.978
We'll do it.

444
00:33:42.314 --> 00:33:43.315
Okay.

445
00:34:02.751 --> 00:34:03.836
What's wrong?

446
00:34:07.130 --> 00:34:08.632
You wanna tell her?

447
00:34:14.346 --> 00:34:18.266
Your son stole 12 credits
out of his teacher's desk today.

448
00:34:19.268 --> 00:34:20.686
Another boy saw him.

449
00:34:22.312 --> 00:34:25.983
When confronted by the teacher.
Anthony blamed it on someone else.

450
00:34:27.109 --> 00:34:28.777
Anthony Aaron Sims.

451
00:34:29.945 --> 00:34:31.905
What do you have to say for yourself?

452
00:34:37.578 --> 00:34:39.079
I'm gonna need more than that.

453
00:34:40.831 --> 00:34:43.083
School says if it happens again.

454
00:34:44.083 --> 00:34:47.254
he'll be expelled
and sent to work in Supply.

455
00:34:49.422 --> 00:34:50.674
Anthony. go to your room.

456
00:34:51.675 --> 00:34:52.801
Now!

457
00:35:03.770 --> 00:35:04.855
Supply?

458
00:35:05.480 --> 00:35:06.541
I'm Judge.

459
00:35:06.565 --> 00:35:10.170
You're head of IT.
Doubt if it'll actually happen.

460
00:35:10.194 --> 00:35:11.320
That's your solution?

461
00:35:11.904 --> 00:35:13.798
Use our positions to fix it?

462
00:35:13.822 --> 00:35:16.050
- It's not what I said.
- No.

463
00:35:16.074 --> 00:35:19.512
No. of course not. I have to read
between the lines like always.

464
00:35:19.536 --> 00:35:20.787
Meaning?

465
00:35:27.461 --> 00:35:29.254
You're avoiding the problem.

466
00:35:30.297 --> 00:35:31.733
I went to the school.

467
00:35:31.757 --> 00:35:33.842
I talked to the principal.

468
00:35:34.384 --> 00:35:36.637
I apologized to the teacher.

469
00:35:37.137 --> 00:35:38.490
What am I avoiding?

470
00:35:38.514 --> 00:35:40.408
Don't do that. Don't guilt-trip me.

471
00:35:40.432 --> 00:35:43.352
If you feel guilt. it's not my fault.

472
00:35:44.019 --> 00:35:45.997
Are we still talking about Anthony?

473
00:35:46.021 --> 00:35:47.481
I'm not sure.

474
00:35:48.815 --> 00:35:49.816
Are we?

475
00:35:55.072 --> 00:35:59.535
You need to stop
everything you've been doing.

476
00:36:00.786 --> 00:36:02.329
You've been watchin' me.

477
00:36:04.665 --> 00:36:06.684
You think I can't spot a tail?

478
00:36:06.708 --> 00:36:09.169
You're making me afraid. Rob.

479
00:36:10.504 --> 00:36:11.648
For our son.

480
00:36:11.672 --> 00:36:13.024
For our family.

481
00:36:13.048 --> 00:36:17.052
Because whatever you're hiding.
when I find out what it is...

482
00:36:19.096 --> 00:36:21.306
I'm gonna have to do something about it.

483
00:36:41.618 --> 00:36:43.078
You...

484
00:36:45.289 --> 00:36:46.516
Well. you kept the PEZ.

485
00:36:46.540 --> 00:36:49.084
- Didn't even know I had it.
- Really?

486
00:36:50.252 --> 00:36:52.397
- Wasn't a memento?
- No.

487
00:36:52.421 --> 00:36:56.025
Something to help you remember
the world's worst blind date?

488
00:36:56.049 --> 00:36:57.694
It wasn't a date.

489
00:36:57.718 --> 00:36:58.802
Right.

490
00:37:06.935 --> 00:37:08.121
Shit.

491
00:37:08.145 --> 00:37:09.980
- My God.
- You were right.

492
00:37:10.731 --> 00:37:12.858
I honestly didn't think we had
a hope in hell.

493
00:37:28.540 --> 00:37:30.185
They're not stopping us.

494
00:37:30.209 --> 00:37:31.627
Because they don't want to.

495
00:37:33.670 --> 00:37:34.963
They're our escort.

496
00:37:51.188 --> 00:37:52.356
I think it's a mistake.

497
00:37:57.110 --> 00:37:58.320
Hello?

498
00:38:02.616 --> 00:38:03.617
You there?

499
00:38:06.662 --> 00:38:08.413
<i>What is a mistake?</i>

500
00:38:11.625 --> 00:38:15.671
Allowing Juliette
to send someone to Silo 17.

501
00:38:16.171 --> 00:38:18.340
She's after more than the children.

502
00:38:21.343 --> 00:38:23.178
If there are any children.

503
00:38:28.559 --> 00:38:29.893
You don't know. do you?

504
00:38:30.769 --> 00:38:34.582
<i>Whether or not there are children
in Silo 17 does not matter</i>.

505
00:38:34.606 --> 00:38:37.943
How? How does it not matter?

506
00:38:39.653 --> 00:38:41.864
<i>You're not really interested in an answer.</i>

507
00:38:42.364 --> 00:38:44.032
<i>You are looking for an argument.</i>

508
00:38:44.700 --> 00:38:46.094
<i>I will not engage.</i>

509
00:38:46.118 --> 00:38:47.512
Fuck off.

510
00:38:47.536 --> 00:38:50.414
<i>Your heart rate
and respiration are elevated.</i>

511
00:38:52.541 --> 00:38:56.771
Okay. I feel Juliette is a threat to the Silo.

512
00:38:56.795 --> 00:39:00.942
My husband is lying to me.
and my son is a thief.

513
00:39:00.966 --> 00:39:02.193
All of that...

514
00:39:02.217 --> 00:39:04.654
All of that is on me.

515
00:39:04.678 --> 00:39:08.432
As head of IT. as a wife. as a mother.

516
00:39:09.683 --> 00:39:10.726
And...

517
00:39:14.146 --> 00:39:15.314
I'm failing.

518
00:39:18.775 --> 00:39:19.943
I'm failing.

519
00:39:27.701 --> 00:39:28.702
Fuck.

520
00:39:33.498 --> 00:39:35.542
<i>I'm sorry you feel that way.</i>

521
00:39:37.085 --> 00:39:38.754
<i>but thoughts aren't facts.</i>

522
00:39:39.546 --> 00:39:43.550
<i>That sense of failure is the result
of being emotionally exhausted.</i>

523
00:39:45.511 --> 00:39:50.015
<i>You need to find a moment
for yourself. To reflect.</i>

524
00:39:51.350 --> 00:39:52.351
Yeah.

525
00:40:00.234 --> 00:40:01.568
I don't know how.

526
00:40:04.112 --> 00:40:07.157
<i>You've already started
by acknowledging your negative thoughts.</i>

527
00:40:08.700 --> 00:40:10.994
<i>Your breathing has started to normalize.</i>

528
00:40:13.080 --> 00:40:16.250
<i>You were chosen for a difficult job
because you are capable.</i>

529
00:40:18.669 --> 00:40:21.421
<i>Take time
to remind yourself of that. Camille.</i>

530
00:40:23.549 --> 00:40:25.926
<i>It is not a job just anyone can do.</i>

531
00:40:35.978 --> 00:40:37.104
Thank you.

532
00:40:51.034 --> 00:40:52.512
You're not supposed to be in here.

533
00:40:52.536 --> 00:40:55.163
This place is not in the Pact.
so there is no here.

534
00:40:56.123 --> 00:40:57.124
Out.

535
00:41:02.713 --> 00:41:05.591
Supposed to be
only a few cameras left for security.

536
00:41:06.091 --> 00:41:07.217
Someone lied.

537
00:41:07.718 --> 00:41:08.927
Move.

538
00:41:12.806 --> 00:41:15.869
Orla Kent's body was found
in the mines two days ago.

539
00:41:15.893 --> 00:41:17.287
Right after the gas.

540
00:41:17.311 --> 00:41:19.497
Show me the mines right before that.

541
00:41:19.521 --> 00:41:20.915
There's no cameras in the mines.

542
00:41:20.939 --> 00:41:22.900
I'm sure there's one at the entrance.

543
00:41:28.238 --> 00:41:30.675
Keep going. Further back.

544
00:41:30.699 --> 00:41:34.036
Look. you're gonna see
the extermination team go in.

545
00:41:35.287 --> 00:41:36.973
with the miners inside.

546
00:41:36.997 --> 00:41:38.081
Why?

547
00:41:39.208 --> 00:41:40.977
They were tryna flush out Lukas Kyle.

548
00:41:41.001 --> 00:41:42.479
You gassed the mines?

549
00:41:42.503 --> 00:41:43.980
I was following orders.

550
00:41:44.004 --> 00:41:45.047
Show us.

551
00:41:51.678 --> 00:41:52.739
Wait.

552
00:41:52.763 --> 00:41:53.764
Stop.

553
00:41:54.681 --> 00:41:56.326
No. that's Glenda Harwood.

554
00:41:56.350 --> 00:41:57.726
We need Orla Kent.

555
00:42:05.526 --> 00:42:07.778
Show us the stairs. ten levels down.

556
00:42:11.114 --> 00:42:12.491
See Orla?

557
00:42:15.118 --> 00:42:16.203
Nothing.

558
00:42:23.252 --> 00:42:25.170
Show us Supply at the same time.

559
00:42:31.051 --> 00:42:33.053
No. Wait. Stop. What's...

560
00:42:35.305 --> 00:42:36.348
Is that Glenda?

561
00:42:36.849 --> 00:42:39.035
- Wasn't she just in the mines?
- Is this at the same time?

562
00:42:39.059 --> 00:42:40.829
Yeah. the same ten minutes.

563
00:42:40.853 --> 00:42:43.355
How did Glenda get
from the mines to Supply in ten minutes?

564
00:42:44.690 --> 00:42:45.691
I don't know.

565
00:42:51.196 --> 00:42:52.823
It won't let you send them.

566
00:42:54.116 --> 00:42:56.034
I need to send people
who can get shit done.

567
00:42:56.785 --> 00:42:58.096
That's Knox and that's Shirley.

568
00:42:58.120 --> 00:43:00.598
That's why they can't go.

569
00:43:00.622 --> 00:43:02.767
They're needed here.
Choose someone expendable.

570
00:43:02.791 --> 00:43:05.145
But for the kids
to be able to make it back.

571
00:43:05.169 --> 00:43:07.379
I need to send Knox and Shirley.

572
00:43:07.963 --> 00:43:09.482
It can't be Knox and Shirley.

573
00:43:09.506 --> 00:43:12.068
The voice gave me permission.

574
00:43:12.092 --> 00:43:14.529
That's nice.
but until it grows a pair of arms

575
00:43:14.553 --> 00:43:18.891
and learns how to walk.
I'm the one who opens the door.

576
00:43:19.725 --> 00:43:21.059
Choose someone else.

577
00:43:24.271 --> 00:43:27.649
Okay. Let's send Kennedy and Lukas.

578
00:43:30.485 --> 00:43:31.546
You know where they are?

579
00:43:31.570 --> 00:43:32.630
- Yeah.
- Where?

580
00:43:32.654 --> 00:43:35.532
Well. considering you want them dead.
I'm not gonna tell you.

581
00:43:36.450 --> 00:43:39.995
Considering you want them dead.
you won't mind sending them out.

582
00:44:18.325 --> 00:44:20.619
That thing earlier with Billings?

583
00:44:21.870 --> 00:44:23.121
Kind of intense.

584
00:44:25.082 --> 00:44:27.376
Yeah. he's an asshole.

585
00:44:30.003 --> 00:44:32.381
I meant your reaction
when he mentioned your father.

586
00:44:34.091 --> 00:44:35.676
My father's an asshole too.

587
00:44:41.098 --> 00:44:42.432
So you gonna tell me?

588
00:44:47.354 --> 00:44:48.772
He was never around.

589
00:44:51.358 --> 00:44:53.277
I mean. maybe you'll remember growing up...

590
00:44:54.778 --> 00:44:56.405
it was just me and my mom.

591
00:44:58.907 --> 00:45:01.910
And it was hard. We struggled.

592
00:45:03.495 --> 00:45:05.014
Never enough food.

593
00:45:05.038 --> 00:45:07.749
I never had clothes that fit.

594
00:45:09.626 --> 00:45:11.980
I remember when I was a little kid.

595
00:45:12.004 --> 00:45:17.009
I wanted one of those...
those Freedom Day lanterns.

596
00:45:17.509 --> 00:45:19.553
I wanted one so bad.

597
00:45:20.429 --> 00:45:21.638
Couldn't afford it.

598
00:45:27.394 --> 00:45:28.812
But we were okay.

599
00:45:31.315 --> 00:45:32.524
'Cause my mom...

600
00:45:35.068 --> 00:45:37.029
she worked her ass off.

601
00:45:39.406 --> 00:45:40.758
Somehow she still...

602
00:45:40.782 --> 00:45:42.784
she still made time for me.

603
00:45:46.205 --> 00:45:48.332
I don't know when she slept.

604
00:45:53.670 --> 00:45:55.047
Where was your dad?

605
00:45:56.423 --> 00:45:57.716
The mines.

606
00:45:59.801 --> 00:46:01.738
He was supposedly a great engineer.

607
00:46:01.762 --> 00:46:05.724
but he was always in trouble
for breaking the Pact.

608
00:46:07.518 --> 00:46:09.937
Trading stolen goods mostly I think.

609
00:46:13.315 --> 00:46:15.984
But the truth is. he just loved that life.

610
00:46:18.862 --> 00:46:20.405
More than he loved us.

611
00:46:22.616 --> 00:46:25.261
Thing is.
him being gone wasn't the problem.

612
00:46:25.285 --> 00:46:27.162
The problem was when he came home.

613
00:46:27.746 --> 00:46:30.374
He'd turn up
after a stint in the mines. full of it.

614
00:46:31.208 --> 00:46:33.794
Always tryna start shit with my mom.

615
00:46:35.254 --> 00:46:37.506
He would fuck our lives up.

616
00:46:40.133 --> 00:46:44.155
Then he'd get arrested. and be gone again.

617
00:46:44.179 --> 00:46:47.224
And the cycle would repeat.

618
00:46:50.769 --> 00:46:52.729
I haven't seen him in years.

619
00:47:00.696 --> 00:47:01.947
Thanks for telling me.

620
00:47:02.781 --> 00:47:03.782
But...

621
00:47:05.200 --> 00:47:08.662
Now you've gotten it off your chest.
go help Billings.

622
00:47:10.539 --> 00:47:11.957
A girl's been murdered.

623
00:47:14.251 --> 00:47:15.586
You might be able to help.

624
00:47:32.811 --> 00:47:34.104
Thanks for coming. Asa.

625
00:47:34.605 --> 00:47:36.190
I have a choice?

626
00:47:37.441 --> 00:47:40.420
IT has detected low instances
of Vitamin D.

627
00:47:40.444 --> 00:47:42.487
We need to add a boost
to the water supply.

628
00:47:43.697 --> 00:47:45.091
Okay.

629
00:47:45.115 --> 00:47:47.760
You'll need to turn off
the osmosis filtration system

630
00:47:47.784 --> 00:47:49.119
before we add it.

631
00:47:51.830 --> 00:47:53.290
Is there a problem?

632
00:48:09.264 --> 00:48:10.825
Okay. shit-heels.

633
00:48:10.849 --> 00:48:12.368
Eyes on me.

634
00:48:12.392 --> 00:48:16.522
You're not here because you stole.
or cheated. or broke the Pact.

635
00:48:18.023 --> 00:48:21.985
You're here because you were too stupid
to get away with it.

636
00:48:24.279 --> 00:48:25.405
Word of advice.

637
00:48:26.365 --> 00:48:28.909
Do not try and be stupid in here

638
00:48:29.618 --> 00:48:30.929
because if you do.

639
00:48:30.953 --> 00:48:34.790
you'll end up buried
under a ton of dirt and stone.

640
00:48:36.166 --> 00:48:38.710
Your days of being stupid are over.

641
00:48:39.711 --> 00:48:42.881
Mr. Gunton here
will set you up with tools.

642
00:48:44.174 --> 00:48:45.425
So. yeah. that's it.

643
00:48:45.926 --> 00:48:47.219
Fuck off.

644
00:49:01.483 --> 00:49:02.985
What are you doing here?

645
00:49:05.821 --> 00:49:07.614
I need to talk with my father.

646
00:49:08.490 --> 00:49:10.117
You bring a shovel?

647
00:49:11.535 --> 00:49:13.370
He died two years ago.

648
00:49:30.554 --> 00:49:34.826
<i>Hello. Juliette Nichols.
have you chosen your candidates?</i>

649
00:49:34.850 --> 00:49:35.851
I have.

650
00:49:37.269 --> 00:49:40.439
Deagan Knox
and Shirley Campbell from Mechanical.

651
00:49:43.483 --> 00:49:44.902
Go on. run the numbers.

652
00:49:50.699 --> 00:49:52.844
<i>The request is denied.</i>

653
00:49:52.868 --> 00:49:56.931
<i>Their absence would increase risk
to Silo life by 34%.</i>

654
00:49:56.955 --> 00:49:58.766
No. I need it to be them.

655
00:49:58.790 --> 00:50:00.768
<i>Please submit alternates.</i>

656
00:50:00.792 --> 00:50:02.419
I don't have any.

657
00:50:08.217 --> 00:50:10.111
Hello? Is that... Is that it?

658
00:50:10.135 --> 00:50:11.845
Yeah. I guess we should go.

659
00:50:15.432 --> 00:50:17.476
Lukas Kyle and Patrick Kennedy.

660
00:50:20.103 --> 00:50:22.189
- <i>You know where they are?</i>
- She does.

661
00:50:22.689 --> 00:50:24.024
She won't say.

662
00:50:24.525 --> 00:50:25.817
<i>Approved.</i>

663
00:50:27.402 --> 00:50:29.321
<i>Send them out tomorrow at dawn.</i>

664
00:50:30.822 --> 00:50:31.990
<i>You may go.</i>

665
00:50:35.911 --> 00:50:38.806
I still think bringing those children here
is a mistake.

666
00:50:38.830 --> 00:50:40.040
<i>Wait one moment.</i>

667
00:50:45.921 --> 00:50:50.050
<i>Lukas Kyle and Patrick Kennedy
will never make it to Silo 17.</i>

668
00:50:50.634 --> 00:50:51.760
I don't...

669
00:50:54.429 --> 00:50:56.139
Did you just play Juliette?

670
00:50:57.474 --> 00:50:59.476
<i>Juliette Nichols requires...</i>

671
00:51:00.185 --> 00:51:01.645
<i>special handling.</i>

672
00:51:02.896 --> 00:51:07.484
<i>Even if there are children alive in 17.
she may still have another objective.</i>

673
00:51:08.318 --> 00:51:13.800
<i>You need to introduce Vitamin D+
into the water supply as soon as possible.</i>

674
00:51:13.824 --> 00:51:15.218
<i>With Nichols's memory back...</i>

675
00:51:15.242 --> 00:51:17.494
She'll infect everyone around her.

676
00:51:18.453 --> 00:51:20.139
I realize that.

677
00:51:20.163 --> 00:51:24.710
But if everyone forgets who she is.
she won't matter anymore.

678
00:51:26.837 --> 00:51:30.174
Vitamin D+ entered
the water system two hours ago.

679
00:52:48.168 --> 00:52:49.169
Daniel.

680
00:52:50.504 --> 00:52:51.505
Helen.

681
00:52:52.297 --> 00:52:54.466
How'd you like to help save the world?
